C Cuts of the K0S analysis k0s (test/src/k0s.f): very loose track selection
C Tracks: minimum number of hits in the r-phi plane, minimum distance to the beam (mm)
NHMIN 4
C Minimum number of selected tracks of an event
NTMIN 2
D0MIN 1.0
C Minimum momentum of a track at the vertex (GeV)
PMIN 0.04
C Minimum momentum of the pair, the K0S candidate (GeV)
PKMIN 0.1
C Pairs of tracks: maximum distance of the helices in (x,y) (mm)
DXYMAX 10.0
C Range of the distance of the vertex from the primary vertex (mm); no upper cut (a very large value)
RVMIN 5.0
RVMAX 1.0E6
C Maximum difference of z of the two tracks at the vertex (mm); no cut (a very large value)
DZMAX 1.0E6
C Minimum cosine of the angle between the momentum of the pair and the direction from the primary vertex to the vertex (3 dimensions)
CPMIN 0.8
C Primary vertex: maximum |z| (mm); an event without a primary vertex is rejected
ZPMAX 200.0
C Fit of the vertex of the two tracks together (1: on) with the assumed errors in (x,y) and in z (mm); maximum chi2 of the fit
FITVTX 1
SIGXY 2.0
SIGZ 20.0
CHIMAX 10.0
STOP
